.DS_Store
.superpowers/
outputs/
work/

# The Reader scaffold ships an outputs/ convention doc, and only that. Re-include the directory so the
# doc is reachable, then re-ignore everything inside it and re-include the doc alone, so a reader that
# has actually produced output cannot surface that output as untracked material in the distribution.
# The blanket outputs/ exclusion above is otherwise unchanged.
!template/reader/outputs/
template/reader/outputs/*
!template/reader/outputs/README.md

# The external QA report of 22 August 2026 is deliberately NOT carried in this repository. It is held
# in the deployment's own records, and the change packages under openspec/ describe it as an external
# report of that date rather than naming a path a reader would try to open.
#
# The reason is mechanical, and it is recorded so that a later maintainer does not "fix" it. The
# canonical leakage guard denylists a term that the report uses in an ordinary English sense, so a
# fail-closed control refuses a push carrying this file. The control is working correctly: it cannot
# tell the two senses apart, and it exists because nobody can eyeball hundreds of denylist entries.
# Editing an external report so that it passes a scan alters evidence, and exempting one term
# weakens a guard that protects everything else. Excluding the file is the option that costs least
# and hides nothing. See the v1.49 version row in STANDARD.md.
/KM-STANDARD-AUDIT-2026-08-22.md
